clang/LLVM: __attribute__((interrupt("WCH-Interrupt-fast"))) for WCH QingKe
cores with the Hardware Prologue/Epilogue (HPE) on.

The core saves ra, t0-t6 and a0-a7 (ra, t0-t2, a0-a5 on RV32E) on entry and
restores them on mret, so the handler saves only the callee-saved and
floating-point registers it uses. Same spelling as WCH's GCC.

