diff -ruN a/clang/include/clang/Basic/AttrDocs.td b/clang/include/clang/Basic/AttrDocs.td
--- a/clang/include/clang/Basic/AttrDocs.td	2026-11-12 07:36:39.311773546 +0900
+++ b/clang/include/clang/Basic/AttrDocs.td	2026-11-12 07:36:57.853820776 +0900
@@ -3232,6 +3232,13 @@
 The SiFive CLIC values may be combined with each other and with the ``machine``
 attribute value. Any other combination of different values is not allowed.
 
+The ``WCH-Interrupt-fast`` value is for WCH's QingKe cores with the Hardware
+Prologue/Epilogue (HPE) enabled: the core itself saves the integer caller-saved
+registers (``ra``, ``t0``-``t6``, ``a0``-``a7``; ``ra``, ``t0``-``t2``,
+``a0``-``a5`` on RV32E) on entry and restores them on ``mret``. The handler
+saves only the callee-saved and floating-point registers it uses. The spelling
+is that of WCH's own GCC, so their example code compiles unchanged.
+
 Repeated interrupt attribute on the same declaration will cause a warning
 to be emitted. In case of repeated declarations, the last one prevails.
 
